--
-- WHY THE EXTRA STEPS IN SECTION 7
--   A person created with plain INSERTs into auth.users cannot sign in, because
--   a normal sign-up also fills in a few other fields and creates a sign-in
--   "identity". The block marked "FILL IN WHAT A NORMAL SIGN-UP WOULD SET" does
--   that. Also, the app creates a blank, pending profile automatically for every
--   new user, so the profile inserts below use DO UPDATE to replace it.
--
-- The very last statement lists every account and says OK, or what is missing.
--
-- It also adds a few sample game notes (needs 20261102100000_add_game_notes.sql) and
-- game day extras: phones, directions, access details, a rainout, a private note and a
-- running-late report (needs 20261104100000_add_game_day_extras.sql), and sample
-- reports (needs 20261105100000_add_reports.sql).
--
-- This file also switches the DEMO CLOCK on (see near the end). It needs the
-- migrations up to 20261101100000_add_demo_clock.sql applied first.
-- ============================================================================

